column3:
This particular hack, yes, but the general point stands. Sometimes hacks make for great code. The point is that <i>this</i> is good code:<p><pre><code>    float h = 0.5f*x;
    int i = *(int*)&x;
    i = 0x5f3759df - (i>>1);
    x = *(float*)&i;
    return x*(1.5f - h*x*x);
</code></pre>
That's 3 local variables, 5 short statements... makes me wonder how quickly one could search/test all combinations of sensible 5-statement functions to find other such "hacks"...
